course: dictionary
lesson: 13202
title: Functional: working and useful
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word functional comes from function, which means the job a thing is meant to do. Something functional works properly and can do its job. «The lift is functional again, so we can ride up to the fifth floor.» The clue is again: it was broken, and now it works.
explain: Functional can also mean plain and practical, not fancy. «The school kitchen is functional: it has ovens, sinks and shelves, but no decorations.» The words but no decorations tell you it is about being useful, not pretty. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: In maths, functional links to a function, a rule that turns each input number into one output number. The clues around the word tell you which meaning fits, so read on before you decide.
fact: Functional means working properly and able to do its job.
fact: «Functional» can also mean made to be useful and practical rather than pretty.
fact: In maths, «functional» means to do with functions, rules that turn each input number into one output number.
fact: Phrases you may meet include fully functional, functional design and functional clothing.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The old printer is still functional and prints every page.» What does functional mean here? | Too heavy to move | *Working properly and able to do its job | Very old and covered in dust | Painted in bright colours
exercise: «The coat is functional: it has big pockets and keeps out the rain, with no fancy buttons.» What does functional suggest? | *Practical and made to be useful | Expensive and rare | Broken and unsafe | Pretty and decorated
exercise: In maths, a function is a rule that turns each input number into one output number. What does functional mean in a maths lesson? | To do with football | Very large numbers only | Having no numbers at all | *To do with functions, the rules that give one output for each input
test: «The bridge is functional again after the repairs, so cars can cross it.» What does functional mean? | *Working again and able to do its job | Closed forever | Painted blue | Made of gold
test: Mia says her new bag is functional. Which sentence shows what she means? | Its sequins sparkle and it is the prettiest bag in the shop | It was bought yesterday from the market | It is the biggest bag ever made, so no one can lift it | *It has zips, strong straps and deep pockets, so it carries books well
exam: Which sentence uses functional correctly? | The rainbow was functional above the hills | The sunset is functional on Tuesdays | *The kettle is functional: it boils water quickly and switches off by itself | Her song was functional and sang in the sky
